course: dictionary
lesson: 7078
title: Patty
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A patty is a flat, round cake of food, often minced meat. You can find its meaning from the words around it. Look for clues like burger, minced or round.
explain: «Menu enfant : steak haché, frites, glace à la vanille - 9,50 €» is a French kids' menu. Steak haché is minced beef, so the patty here is a flat round cake of meat. Even if you do not read French, the price, the chips and the ice cream tell you it is a meal.
explain: The same word can mean different things. A burger patty is meat, a Jamaican patty is a pastry with a spicy filling, and a peppermint patty is a small flat sweet. Always ask: what would fit in this sentence? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A patty is a flat, round cake of minced meat or other food.
fact: A patty can also be a small pie or pastry, such as a Jamaican patty with a spicy filling.
fact: In the US, a patty can be a small flat sweet, as in a peppermint patty.
fact: Burger patties can be beef, chicken, veggie or bean.
fact: Kitchen safety: cook meat patties right through so they are not pink in the middle. In the French menu, 9,50 € uses a comma where English uses a decimal point, so it means 9 euros and 50 cents.
exercise: In «Menu enfant : steak haché, frites, glace à la vanille - 9,50 €», what is the steak haché? | A sweet vanilla ice cream | *A minced-beef patty | A slice of chicken | A bowl of soup
exercise: Which meaning fits a Jamaican patty? | A bowl of rice | *A small pie or pastry with a spicy filling | A cake of bread for toast | A small sweet, like a peppermint
exercise: In the French menu, 9,50 € uses a comma. What does the comma mean? | *A decimal point, so it means 9 euros and 50 cents | A full stop that ends the sentence | A list separator for 9 and 50 | A dollar sign
test: In «The chef shaped the minced beef into a round, flat patty», what is a patty? | *A flat round cake of food | A pair of shoes | A small wooden bowl | A loud noise
test: Ella says a patty is always a burger. Is she right? | *No, a patty can also be a small pie, as in a Jamaican patty | Yes, but only in France | Yes, because a patty is only ever in a burger
exam: Why must meat patties be cooked right through? | *So they are not pink in the middle | To make them sweeter | To make them taller | So they can be sold as sweets
